{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task SE-PE-01. I need to write a `solve(case)` function that:\n\n1. Takes a payload with `nodes` and `required_symbols`\n2. Returns `{\"removed_node_ids\": [...], \"retained_node_ids\": [...]}`\n\nLet me understand the problem from the fixtures:\n\nEach node has:\n- `id`: unique identifier\n- `parent`: parent node id (null for root)\n- `symbol`: a symbol name\n- `depth`: depth in tree\n- `removable`: whether the node can be removed\n- `utility`: a float value\n\nThe `required_symbols` list specifies symbols that must be retained.\n\nThe task seems to be about pruning a tree while keeping nodes that:\n1. Are not removable (must be retained)\n2. Have required symbols (their subtree must be retained)\n\nLet me think more carefully. The key question is: what determines which nodes are removed vs retained?\n\nLooking at the fixtures:\n- `required_symbols`: [\"root\", \"s1\"] in all cases\n\nNodes with non-removable flag must be retained. Nodes whose symbol is in required_symbols must also be retained. But what about ancestors of required nodes?\n\nLet me think about this differently. In a tree pruning scenario:\n- A node is retained if it's non-removable OR its symbol is required\n- But if a node is retained, its ancestors must also be retained (to keep the path to root)\n- If a node is removed, all its descendants are also removed\n\nWait, but removable=false nodes might still need to be checked against required symbols.\n\nLet me re-read: `removable` is a separate field from required_symbols. A node with `removable=false` cannot be removed regardless. A node whose symbol is in `required_symbols` should be retained.\n\nThe logic might be:\n1. A node MUST be retained if `removable=false`\n2. A node MUST be retained if its symbol is in `required_symbols`\n3. If a node is retained, all its ancestors must be retained\n4. A node CAN be removed if it's `removable=true` AND its subtree contains no required/non-removable nodes\n\nActually wait - let me think about this more carefully. The task is about \"pruning\" a tree. The goal might be to remove nodes that are removable and whose entire subtree can be removed.\n\nA node is \"safe to remove\" if:\n- It is `removable=true`\n- None of its descendants (including itself) are required (non-removable or have required symbol)\n\nLet me verify with case 000:\n- nodes: root(non-removable, symbol=root), n1(non-removable, s1), n2(removable, s2), n3(non-removable, s0), n4(removable, s1), n5(non-removable, s2), n6(removable, s0)\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nTree structure:\n- root → n1, n2, n3\n- n1 → n6\n- n2 → n4\n- n3 → n5\n\nNon-removable nodes: root, n1, n3, n5\nRequired symbol nodes: root (root), n1 (s1), n4 (s1)\n\nn4 has symbol s1 which is required. n4 is removable=true but its symbol is required. So n4 must be retained? But n4 is under n2 which is removable...\n\nHmm, but if n4 must be retained, then n2 (its parent) must also be retained.\n\nWait, maybe the logic is:\n- A node is retained if: it's non-removable OR its symbol is in required_symbols OR it has a descendant that must be retained\n- A node is removed if: it's removable AND none of its descendants need to be retained\n\nLet me trace case 000:\n- n4: removable=true, symbol=s1 (required) → retained\n- n2: removable=true, symbol=s2, but has descendant n4 which is retained → retained\n- n6: removable=true, symbol=s0 (not required), no children → removable. But wait, parent n1 is non-removable. Does that matter?\n\nActually n6 being a child of a non-removable node doesn't make n6 non-removable. n6 itself is removable=true, has symbol s0 (not required), has no children → should be removed.\n\nSo removed: n6\nRetained: root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5\n\nBut wait, I don't have the expected outputs to verify. Let me think about this differently.\n\nThe algorithm:\n1. Mark a node as \"must retain\" if: removable=false OR symbol in required_symbols\n2. For each \"must retain\" node, mark all ancestors as \"must retain\" (propagate up)\n3. All nodes not marked \"must retain\" are removed (but only if they're removable - non-removable nodes must always be retained)\n\nWait, non-removable nodes are always retained regardless. Let me reformulate:\n\nA node is retained if ANY of:\n- removable=false\n- symbol is in required_symbols\n- has any descendant that is retained\n\nA node is removed if:\n- removable=true AND symbol not in required_symbols AND no descendant is retained\n\nLet me trace case 000:\nLeaves: n4 (s1, required → retained), n5 (non-removable → retained), n6 (removable, s0, no children → removed)\n\nn1's children: n6 (removed). n1 is non-removable → retained.\nn2's children: n4 (retained). n2 is removable but has retained descendant → retained.\nn3's children: n5 (retained). n3 is non-removable → retained (also has retained child).\n\nroot: non-removable, all children evaluated → retained.\n\nSo case 000 result: removed=[n6], retained=[root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5]\n\nCase 001: Same tree structure, same required_symbols.\nn4: removable=true, s1 (required) → retained\nn6: removable=true, s0, no children → removed\nSame result: removed=[n6], retained=[root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5]\n\nCase 002: Same structure, same required_symbols.\nSame logic applies.\nn4: removable=true, s1 (required) → retained\nn6: removable=true, s0, no children → removed\nSame result: removed=[n6], retained=[root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5]\n\nAll three cases seem to have the same result. That makes sense since the structure and removable/symbol attributes are the same, just utilities differ.\n\nNow let me write the solve function:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build node map and children map\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Determine retained nodes using DFS post-order\n    retained = set()\n    \n    def is_retained(node_id):\n        node = node_map[node_id]\n        # Non-removable nodes are always retained\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            retained.add(node_id)\n            # Still need to check children (they might be removable)\n            for child_id in children[node_id]:\n                is_retained(child_id)\n            return True\n        \n        # Check if symbol is required\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            retained.add(node_id)\n            for child_id in children[node_id]:\n                is_retained(child_id)\n            return True\n        \n        # Check if any child must be retained\n        child_retained = any(is_retained(child_id) for child_id in children[node_id])\n        if child_retained:\n            retained.add(node_id)\n            return True\n        \n        return False\n    \n    # Find root(s) - nodes with parent=null\n    roots = [n[\"id\"] for n in nodes if n[\"parent\"] is None]\n    for root_id in roots:\n        is_retained(root_id)\n    \n    # Build result\n    all_ids = [n[\"id\"] for n in nodes]\n    retained_list = [nid for nid in all_ids if nid in retained]\n    removed_list = [nid for nid in all_ids if nid not in retained]\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_list,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_list\n    }\n```\n\nWait, there's a problem with the recursive approach - if a node is non-removable or has a required symbol, I should still check all children (some may still be removed). Let me reconsider.\n\nActually the issue is: when a node has a required symbol or is non-removable, it's retained, but its children might still be removable and removed if they don't themselves meet the criteria.\n\nLet me restructure:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build maps\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Post-order DFS: returns True if this subtree has any retained node\n    # A node is retained if:\n    # 1. removable=false, OR\n    # 2. symbol in required_symbols, OR  \n    # 3. has a retained child\n    retained = set()\n    \n    def process(node_id):\n        node = node_map[node_id]\n        children_retain = False\n        for child_id in children[node_id]:\n            if process(child_id):\n                children_retain = True\n        \n        must_keep = (not node[\"removable\"]) or (node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols) or children_retain\n        if must_keep:\n            retained.add(node_id)\n        return must_keep\n    \n    roots = [n[\"id\"] for n in nodes if n[\"parent\"] is None]\n    for root_id in roots:\n        process(root_id)\n    \n    all_ids = [n[\"id\"] for n in nodes]\n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": [nid for nid in all_ids if nid not in retained],\n        \"retained_node_ids\": [nid for nid in all_ids if nid in retained]\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks cleaner. Let me verify with case 000:\n\nTree:\n- root → n1, n2, n3\n- n1 → n6\n- n2 → n4\n- n3 → n5\n\nProcessing:\n- n6: removable=true, s0 (not required), no children → not retained\n- n1: removable=false → retained (children_retain=false but removable=false)\n- n4: removable=true, s1 (required) → retained\n- n2: removable=true, s2 (not required), children_retain=true (n4 retained) → retained\n- n5: removable=false → retained\n- n3: removable=false → retained\n- root: removable=false → retained\n\nretained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\nremoved = {n6}\n\nThat looks correct.\n\nLet me also consider edge cases:\n- What if a non-removable node has all removable children that aren't required? The non-removable node is retained, children are removed.\n- What about the order of returned IDs? I'm preserving the input order which seems reasonable.\n\nThe solution looks good. Let me write the final JSON response.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Build node map and children map\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    retained = set()\\n\\n    def process(node_id):\\n        node = node_map[node_id]\\n        # Process children first (post-order)\\n        children_retain = False\\n        for child_id in children[node_id]:\\n            if process(child_id):\\n                children_retain = True\\n\\n        # A node is retained if:\\n        # 1. it is non-removable, OR\\n        # 2. its symbol is in required_symbols, OR\\n        # 3. at least one of its descendants is retained\\n        must_keep = (\\n            not node[\\\"removable\\\"]\\n            or node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols\\n            or children_retain\\n        )\\n        if must_keep:\\n            retained.add(node_id)\\n        return must_keep\\n\\n    # Process from each root (parent is null)\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is None:\\n            process(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Preserve original input order\\n    all_ids = [n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes]\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": [nid for nid in all_ids if nid not in retained],\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": [nid for nid in all_ids if nid in retained],\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01KDfx8YAmXSuQ4oHcDqTYDH","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2208},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2208,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":69,"output_tokens":3268,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2822},"service_tier":"standard"}}